# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS TO STOP GCLOUD GUESSING. With no .gcloudignore, gcloud falls
# back to .gitignore — and the repository's .gitignore excludes `.*`, which means
# .dockerignore itself would not be uploaded. The build would then run without
# it, copy a Windows node_modules into the image, and fail on sharp. The failure
# would be a mystifying one, so the fix is to be explicit.
#
# Deliberately near-identical to .dockerignore. The difference is that this one
# governs what leaves the laptop, and .dockerignore governs what enters the
# image; keeping them in step is what makes a local `docker build` and a Cloud
# Build produce the same thing.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

.env
.env.*

tests
.vscode
.idea
